maintainer_comments.body:
In many places, this function is called with an index that at least on first sight looks unbounded, e.g. in acl.c:

```c
        for (int j = 2; j < c->argc; j++) {
            redactClientCommandArgument(c, j);
        }
```

An alternative is to just skip redacting if it's out of range. Bus skipping better than asserting? 🤔
